F5-CEILING patch proposal: generator drops reverse-direction works_for team members
==============================================================================
Branch: fyd-factory (PING repo /home/nolan/projects/ping). NOT APPLIED.
Read-only investigation; apply deliberately.

PROBLEM
-------
The eligibility module (src/fyd/builder/eligibility.ts) counts a team when a
person object links to the owner via works_for "in either direction", and its
report marked coppersmith-plumbing team=1 / People eligible. But the spec
generator (src/fyd/proceduralize/generator.ts :: group()) only matches
owner-as-subject edges with predicates employs|has_member, so the person that
website ingestion recorded as person -> works_for -> business never enters the
people group, no People section is emitted, and the planner (which correctly
filters by the eligibility report) has nothing to keep. Two modules disagree
on the same predicate vocabulary; the narrower one wins silently.

Evidence (F5-CEILING run 2026-09-23, ~/workspace/fyd-factory/ceiling/):
- coppersmith fixture relationship rel-8627fe1497c235f5:
  subject=website-business-2f1327c09d622175-person-377048d67856,
  predicate=works_for, object=website-business-2f1327c09d622175 (the owner).
- deriveEligibility(coppersmith graph): team=1, People eligible.
- planSite(coppersmith graph): home page has NO People section; about page has
  none either. Fingerprint identical to happy-place (which has no people at
  all): composite similarity 1.000, exact home sequence.
- happy-place-rich fixture (employs direction, team=2) DOES emit People on
  home + about. Same component, same planner: only the edge direction differs.

FIX (generator boundary only; no planner/renderer/resolver changes)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
1. group(): merge reverse-direction works_for persons into the people group,
   mirroring eligibility's rule. Deterministic: dedup by id, re-sort by id.
2. Emit People sections with kind:"reference" + the grouped ids instead of the
   owner-centric roleQuery("person"). Resolvers (planner resolveQueryObjects,
   renderer resolveQuery, render-model) all handle "reference" and cannot
   reach reverse-direction members through "related" (they require
   r.subject === from). The resolved set is exactly the grouped team.
3. Bump SITE_PLANNER_VERSION to fyd-site-planner@2: emitted spec bytes change
   (section query kind), and the version stamp exists precisely to mark that.

EXPECTED EFFECT
---------------
- coppersmith-plumbing gains a People section (home + about), bound to the
  works_for person. Its fingerprint diverges from happy-place exactly where
  the entities diverge: variation for the right reason.
- happy-place-rich (employs direction) resolves the same person set as
  before; only the query encoding changes (related -> reference).
- No other site changes: services/products/locations/posts paths untouched.

VERIFICATION (to run after applying)
-------------------------------------
- tsx fingerprint harness: coppersmith People section present with
  objectIds=[person id]; happy-place resolved sets unchanged.
- jest: src/fyd/proceduralize, src/fyd/builder, src/fyd/sitespec suites.
- tsc clean.

